sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant I as Idempotency interceptor
    participant L as TransferService
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    participant W as Outbox worker
    participant E as Consumer

    C->>I: POST /v1/transfers + Idempotency-Key
    I->>D: BEGIN
    I->>D: INSERT idempotency_keys ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING

    alt key already exists
        D-->>I: 0 rows (blocks until the original commits)
        I->>D: SELECT stored response
        I-->>C: 201 + Idempotent-Replay: true
    else key claimed
        I->>L: run handler inside the same transaction
        L->>D: SELECT accounts WHERE id = ANY(...) ORDER BY id FOR UPDATE
        Note over L,D: ascending id order — no A→B / B→A deadlock
        L->>D: SUM entries for both accounts (index-only)
        Note over L: balance check happens under the lock
        L->>D: INSERT transactions
        L->>D: INSERT ledger_entries (both sides)
        L->>D: INSERT outbox_events
        I->>D: UPDATE idempotency_keys SET response
        I->>D: COMMIT
        Note over D: deferred triggers validate the entry set here
        I-->>C: 201 + balances
    end

    W->>D: lease due events (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED), COMMIT
    Note over W,D: no transaction is held open across the network call
    W->>E: POST webhook, HMAC signed
    alt delivered
        W->>D: mark PUBLISHED
    else transient failure
        W->>D: attempts + 1, next_attempt_at += jittered backoff
    else 4xx or attempts exhausted
        W->>D: mark FAILED — dead letter, never auto-deleted
    end
